      "rationale": "1,000 seed money is granted because tutorial quest 1 is itself building a 1,000-won T1 factory \u2014 without seed money the player could not even start the quest chain (chicken-and-egg)."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_design_00_onboarding_tutorial_quest_chain",
      "label": "5-Step Tutorial Quest Chain",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "docs/design/00-onboarding.md",
      "source_location": "L18-L57",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Quests run strictly in order with no skipping so the player is walked through the entire core loop. Known defect (contradiction 11): quest 4 requires 3,000 won for an upgrade but the player holds only ~2,000 at that point, because quest 3 completes on market LISTING not on an actual sale."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_design_00_onboarding_material_base_price",
      "label": "Material Base Price Table (T1/T2/T3)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "docs/design/00-onboarding.md",
      "source_location": "L71-L107",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Base prices are set so every T1 factory converges to 300-400 won per tick, giving a uniform ~3.3-tick (33 min) break-even on the 1,000-won build cost. Direct-purchase price, upgrade cost sanity, and market clamps all derive from this table."
    }
  ],
